1
00:00:09,754 --> 00:00:12,872
This is Part 3 of 6: What it is for.

2
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:18,872
In Parts 1 and 2 I asked whether dependent
arising is as plain as it sounds,

3
00:00:18,952 --> 00:00:22,473
and set out what it says:
no power in the cause,

4
00:00:22,553 --> 00:00:27,378
no doer behind the doing, whatever
appears singled out and designated,

5
00:00:27,458 --> 00:00:31,051
and conditions that are the
appearing itself, not a web.

6
00:00:31,853 --> 00:00:34,318
Now the other question. What is it for?

7
00:00:35,189 --> 00:00:38,329
First, there are two ways
of knowing rightly here.

8
00:00:38,409 --> 00:00:40,140
It helps not to collapse them.

9
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:44,504
The first works through
concepts, within the framework.

10
00:00:44,584 --> 00:00:48,580
Dependent arising is how the
whole of Indra's net comes about.

11
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:51,053
The net is conventional and empty.

12
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:54,151
It keeps presenting
itself upon conditions,

13
00:00:54,231 --> 00:00:57,376
within the framework,
for functional purposes.

14
00:00:58,206 --> 00:00:59,838
This is not a lesser knowing.

15
00:00:59,918 --> 00:01:03,371
It is how a doctor
treats, how a cook cooks,

16
00:01:03,451 --> 00:01:07,270
how a promise is kept,
how karma is understood.

17
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:11,360
In this mode, dependent
arising also shows emptiness.

18
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:15,196
It corrects the inherent reading
from inside the framework.

19
00:01:16,018 --> 00:01:19,158
The second is freedom
from all elaborations.

20
00:01:19,238 --> 00:01:21,332
It is not within the framework at all.

21
00:01:21,412 --> 00:01:23,126
Nothing reified is added.

22
00:01:23,206 --> 00:01:28,633
Nothing is cut into before and after,
part and whole, cause and effect.

23
00:01:29,462 --> 00:01:32,698
Without the framework, there
is one complete stroke.

24
00:01:32,778 --> 00:01:37,521
One here does not mean one stuff,
the oneness of a refined non-dual.

25
00:01:37,601 --> 00:01:38,866
It means not cut up.

26
00:01:38,946 --> 00:01:42,833
The colour is still the colour,
and the sound is still the sound,

27
00:01:42,913 --> 00:01:46,805
each with its own conditions,
and nothing they are all made of.

28
00:01:47,621 --> 00:01:50,788
Not within the framework
does not mean somewhere else.

29
00:01:50,868 --> 00:01:54,511
It means not known by cutting
the appearing into concepts.

30
00:01:54,591 --> 00:01:57,763
It is the same appearing,
known without the cutting.

31
00:01:58,569 --> 00:02:00,269
Neither cancels the other.

32
00:02:00,349 --> 00:02:02,701
The first is not a ladder to throw away.

33
00:02:02,781 --> 00:02:06,374
The second is not a place
outside the world to retreat to.

34
00:02:06,517 --> 00:02:10,160
Freedom from elaborations,
kept apart from the framework,

35
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:12,252
would become a new ground.

36
00:02:12,332 --> 00:02:17,184
That is why, after it, the taste
is met again inside the framework,

37
00:02:17,264 --> 00:02:21,183
in ordinary life, with the
parts and conditions now light.

38
00:02:21,997 --> 00:02:24,716
So the framework can be held three ways.

39
00:02:24,796 --> 00:02:27,107
Without it: one complete stroke.

40
00:02:27,187 --> 00:02:30,531
Within it, with the wisdom
of dependent arising:

41
00:02:30,611 --> 00:02:33,642
the same parts and conditions, now light.

42
00:02:33,722 --> 00:02:38,194
And in between, where we mostly
live: within it, reified.

43
00:02:38,274 --> 00:02:40,372
That middle one is the matrix.

44
00:02:41,190 --> 00:02:45,490
Within the framework, dependent
arising does three kinds of work.

45
00:02:46,293 --> 00:02:50,561
It explains. It answers the
question: how does this come about?

46
00:02:50,641 --> 00:02:52,875
These conditions, met together.

47
00:02:53,689 --> 00:02:54,981
It dismantles.

48
00:02:55,061 --> 00:02:59,478
Because a thing arises in dependence,
it is not there from its own side.

49
00:02:59,558 --> 00:03:02,957
So dependence is the reason
that takes apart the self,

50
00:03:03,037 --> 00:03:06,897
the object, the cause,
the whole, the field,

51
00:03:06,977 --> 00:03:11,421
the substrate, energy and
the web, and shows emptiness.

52
00:03:11,501 --> 00:03:15,366
Tsongkhapa's tradition calls
it the king of reasons.

53
00:03:16,181 --> 00:03:17,894
And it describes the taste.

54
00:03:17,974 --> 00:03:22,718
Seen through, it is the taste
itself: nothing standing on its own,

55
00:03:22,798 --> 00:03:23,998
nothing missing.

56
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:28,814
The three hang together. It can
dismantle because it explains.

57
00:03:28,894 --> 00:03:32,278
What validly depends cannot
also stand by itself.

58
00:03:32,358 --> 00:03:35,729
So the reasoning does not
destroy the world it takes apart.

59
00:03:35,809 --> 00:03:38,397
What goes is only the "from its own side".

60
00:03:39,229 --> 00:03:42,885
Nāgārjuna joins all three in one verse.

61
00:03:42,965 --> 00:03:46,363
What arises in dependence
is what we call emptiness.

62
00:03:46,443 --> 00:03:48,660
That is a designation in dependence.

63
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:50,784
And that itself is the middle way.

64
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:53,727
Two guards go with the dismantling.

65
00:03:53,807 --> 00:03:56,445
It puts nothing in place
of what it removes,

66
00:03:56,525 --> 00:03:59,570
or emptiness becomes the
next thing to hinge on.

67
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:04,515
And it dismantles itself too, since
dependence is not found from its own side

68
00:04:04,595 --> 00:04:09,574
either. A reason held as the final
truth would be one more construct.

69
00:04:10,389 --> 00:04:13,148
Dependent arising is an enlightened view.

70
00:04:13,228 --> 00:04:16,871
By that I do not mean a view
only the enlightened can hold.

71
00:04:16,951 --> 00:04:21,441
I mean the right view of how things
are, which we do not yet live in.

72
00:04:22,249 --> 00:04:25,063
We live reading the matrix as inherent.

73
00:04:25,143 --> 00:04:28,813
Things seem to stand by
themselves. Causes seem to push.

74
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:31,340
A self seems to sit behind the seeing.

75
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,622
That seeming is not a thought we hold.

76
00:04:33,702 --> 00:04:38,016
It is a deep habit of seeing,
in the body, before thought.

77
00:04:38,837 --> 00:04:42,384
Have a second thought. If you
think you do not think inherently,

78
00:04:42,464 --> 00:04:43,829
have a second thought.

79
00:04:44,649 --> 00:04:49,501
Toss the apple again. Do you first
meet a hardness, a red and an arc,

80
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:51,675
and only then put "apple" on them?

81
00:04:51,755 --> 00:04:56,598
Or is the solid apple simply there,
out there, before any thought at all?

82
00:04:57,424 --> 00:05:00,156
For almost all of us, it is simply there.

83
00:05:00,236 --> 00:05:01,855
That is the habit at work.

84
00:05:01,935 --> 00:05:03,662
It does not announce itself.

85
00:05:03,742 --> 00:05:05,541
It is just the way things look.

86
00:05:06,353 --> 00:05:10,091
So agreeing with dependent
arising is not living in it.

87
00:05:10,171 --> 00:05:13,542
We do not live in the
wisdom of dependent arising.

88
00:05:13,622 --> 00:05:18,406
We live in the confusion of thinking,
analysing and orienting ourselves with

89
00:05:18,486 --> 00:05:22,378
inherent thoughts, habitually
and without knowing it.

90
00:05:23,181 --> 00:05:28,060
Even "I do not think inherently"
is usually held the same way,

91
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:31,443
as a fact about a self
standing behind the thought.

92
00:05:31,523 --> 00:05:33,209
It is Feynman's quip again.

93
00:05:33,289 --> 00:05:35,768
If you think you understand, you don't.

94
00:05:36,577 --> 00:05:38,743
So I keep two frameworks apart.

95
00:05:39,570 --> 00:05:42,996
The default framework is the
conventional cutting itself:

96
00:05:43,076 --> 00:05:48,580
parts and whole, before and after,
cause and effect, agent and action.

97
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:53,254
It works. We need it to speak,
to cook and to keep promises.

98
00:05:53,334 --> 00:05:55,541
Dependent arising lives here.

99
00:05:55,671 --> 00:05:57,004
"How does this come about?"

100
00:05:57,084 --> 00:06:01,900
Only this framework can ask that,
and dependent arising is its answer.

101
00:06:02,721 --> 00:06:06,934
The inherent framework is the habit of
taking what the cutting singles out as

102
00:06:07,014 --> 00:06:10,154
standing by itself. That is the matrix.

103
00:06:10,234 --> 00:06:13,651
Not a world, not a
field. A habit of seeing.

104
00:06:14,474 --> 00:06:18,076
This does not mean we live in
a matrix and must escape it.

105
00:06:18,156 --> 00:06:22,030
The framework of parts and
conditions is not what binds us.

106
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:25,536
What binds us is living in
it with reified thoughts,

107
00:06:25,616 --> 00:06:30,848
taking the parts, the conditions and the
sequence to be there from their own side.

108
00:06:30,928 --> 00:06:33,783
Dependent arising is not the matrix.

109
00:06:33,863 --> 00:06:36,718
It is the wisdom that shows the matrix up.

110
00:06:36,798 --> 00:06:38,801
The framework is not the prison.

111
00:06:39,617 --> 00:06:44,034
Dependent arising lives in the
first and unbinds the second.

112
00:06:44,114 --> 00:06:49,442
Run the two together, and "dependent
arising lives in a framework" is heard as

113
00:06:49,522 --> 00:06:52,571
"dependent arising is only a story".

114
00:06:52,674 --> 00:06:55,057
That is the slide into annihilation.

115
00:06:55,869 --> 00:06:58,574
And living in the
framework with this wisdom,

116
00:06:58,654 --> 00:07:03,656
I begin to see that even spontaneous
presence can be understood within it.

117
00:07:03,736 --> 00:07:08,560
Crudely and clumsily, because the
framework still speaks in pieces and in

118
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,816
sequence. But truly.

119
00:07:10,896 --> 00:07:14,022
Conditions are the appearing.
Nothing produces it.

120
00:07:14,102 --> 00:07:16,590
It is complete as its conditions meet.

121
00:07:16,670 --> 00:07:21,020
It is not a place beyond concepts,
waiting outside the framework.

122
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,831
That would make it a new ground.

123
00:07:23,654 --> 00:07:28,330
How is that different from reading a taste
through a concept, which I warn against?

124
00:07:28,410 --> 00:07:31,876
The difference is not
concepts. It is reification.

125
00:07:31,956 --> 00:07:37,786
When the concepts are taken as found, the
taste is fixed into a self or a source.

126
00:07:37,866 --> 00:07:42,691
Held as designations, the same
concepts point and do not fix.

127
00:07:42,771 --> 00:07:45,245
Understanding is still not the taste.

128
00:07:45,325 --> 00:07:47,397
It is the taste understood rightly.

129
00:07:48,197 --> 00:07:51,609
Now, ignorance. Ignorance
is not a power either.

130
00:07:51,689 --> 00:07:54,503
It is not a thing in us
with a force to blind.

131
00:07:54,583 --> 00:07:57,804
It is a very deep habit
of confused seeing,

132
00:07:57,884 --> 00:08:01,894
designated as ignorance, and
not found when searched for.

133
00:08:01,974 --> 00:08:06,011
It blinds reliably because its
conditions keep being renewed.

134
00:08:06,091 --> 00:08:09,425
And it can end, because
nothing stands behind it.

135
00:08:10,246 --> 00:08:14,405
Some readings say dependent
arising originates with ignorance,

136
00:08:14,485 --> 00:08:16,661
since the twelve links begin there.

137
00:08:16,741 --> 00:08:18,509
That reading needs refining.

138
00:08:18,589 --> 00:08:24,288
Dependent arising as a view originates
as the corrective antidote for ignorance.

139
00:08:25,093 --> 00:08:29,768
If it simply came from ignorance, it
would be odd to praise it as the supreme

140
00:08:29,848 --> 00:08:32,531
teaching. Yet that is what the texts do.

141
00:08:33,329 --> 00:08:38,670
Nāgārjuna opens his Fundamental Verses by
bowing to the Buddha who taught dependent

142
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:44,077
arising: without arising or ceasing,
the stilling of elaborations,

143
00:08:44,157 --> 00:08:49,662
peace. Candrakīrti opens his Clear
Words by unpacking that homage.

144
00:08:49,742 --> 00:08:53,154
Tsongkhapa praises the
Buddha for this one teaching,

145
00:08:53,234 --> 00:08:58,249
the best of all he taught, and says that
seeing it reverses the root of the round

146
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:01,256
of birth and death, which is ignorance.

147
00:09:02,061 --> 00:09:07,035
And the Buddha himself: whoever sees
dependent arising sees the Dhamma;

148
00:09:07,115 --> 00:09:10,527
whoever sees the Dhamma
sees dependent arising.

149
00:09:10,607 --> 00:09:13,326
It stands whether or not buddhas arise.

150
00:09:13,406 --> 00:09:15,921
Not as a law kept somewhere behind things,

151
00:09:16,001 --> 00:09:18,462
but because this is how appearing is.

152
00:09:18,542 --> 00:09:21,156
So it is not something
ignorance produced either.

153
00:09:21,974 --> 00:09:24,598
The twelve links do begin with ignorance,

154
00:09:24,678 --> 00:09:27,057
and none of these masters denies it.

155
00:09:27,137 --> 00:09:29,113
They read the links two ways.

156
00:09:29,230 --> 00:09:32,750
Forward, from ignorance
to old age and death,

157
00:09:32,830 --> 00:09:35,848
the links show how the
round of suffering runs.

158
00:09:35,928 --> 00:09:39,924
In reverse, from ignorance
ceasing to suffering ceasing,

159
00:09:40,004 --> 00:09:41,663
they show how it ends.

160
00:09:41,743 --> 00:09:43,606
No one praises ignorance.

161
00:09:43,686 --> 00:09:45,975
They praise the seeing that undoes it.

162
00:09:46,781 --> 00:09:51,782
One last knot. I have read more than
once that conventional truth is a veil,

163
00:09:51,862 --> 00:09:56,257
so dependent arising, being
conventional, must be the veil.

164
00:09:57,070 --> 00:10:01,922
The source is genuine. The Sanskrit
word for conventional, saṃvṛti,

165
00:10:02,002 --> 00:10:06,189
can mean a covering. Candrakīrti
gives it three meanings.

166
00:10:06,269 --> 00:10:11,447
Concealment, the ignorance that hides
how things are. Mutual dependence.

167
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:16,220
And worldly convention, the
designations by which the world speaks.

168
00:10:17,029 --> 00:10:20,074
Read carefully, this
supports the refinement.

169
00:10:20,154 --> 00:10:22,968
What veils is ignorance, the concealer.

170
00:10:23,048 --> 00:10:26,568
Dependent arising is the second
meaning of the same word,

171
00:10:26,648 --> 00:10:28,402
and designation the third.

172
00:10:28,482 --> 00:10:30,617
Concealment is the matrix.

173
00:10:30,697 --> 00:10:33,484
Mutual dependence is dependent arising.

174
00:10:33,564 --> 00:10:36,532
Worldly convention is
the default framework.

175
00:10:37,350 --> 00:10:39,852
The same appearance can be held two ways.

176
00:10:39,932 --> 00:10:43,466
Held by the concealer, it
seems to stand by itself,

177
00:10:43,546 --> 00:10:45,613
and that seeming is the veil.

178
00:10:45,693 --> 00:10:50,277
Seen as dependent arising, it is
the seeing that lifts the veil.

179
00:10:51,093 --> 00:10:53,880
Candrakīrti says as much himself.

180
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,950
For those who have abandoned
afflictive ignorance,

181
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:59,260
things appear like reflections.

182
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:03,621
They are not truths for them, because
they no longer fix on them as real.

183
00:11:03,701 --> 00:11:05,388
He calls this mere convention.

184
00:11:05,468 --> 00:11:09,138
Still appearing, still
working, no longer veiling.

185
00:11:09,218 --> 00:11:12,915
The conventional, read
with ignorance, veils.

186
00:11:12,995 --> 00:11:15,052
With wisdom, why would it veil?

187
00:11:15,865 --> 00:11:18,556
Other readings deserve
to be stated fairly.

188
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:22,986
Gorampa and the Sakya school,
as they are commonly read,

189
00:11:23,066 --> 00:11:27,904
and some Kagyu and Dzogchen teachers,
define the conventional as what appears to

190
00:11:27,984 --> 00:11:32,089
mistaken cognition. Then
convention veils by definition.

191
00:11:32,169 --> 00:11:36,464
That is a deliberate choice of meaning,
taking the first meaning as the whole

192
00:11:36,544 --> 00:11:37,266
word.

193
00:11:37,346 --> 00:11:41,618
Where I differ is in giving dependence
and designation their own place.

194
00:11:42,437 --> 00:11:47,071
In Tsongkhapa's tradition, things can
still appear as standing by themselves

195
00:11:47,151 --> 00:11:52,601
after ignorance is no longer believed,
as a subtle obscuration that lasts until

196
00:11:52,681 --> 00:11:55,767
buddhahood. That does not
contradict what I say.

197
00:11:55,847 --> 00:11:58,281
It is the habit of seeing inherently.

198
00:11:58,361 --> 00:12:00,590
The veil of belief goes first.

199
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:03,747
The veil of habitual
appearance thins in time.

200
00:12:04,569 --> 00:12:09,434
And even held without ignorance, the
framework is still an elaboration,

201
00:12:09,514 --> 00:12:14,040
compared with freedom from all
elaborations. That is not a veil.

202
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:16,124
It is the other mode of right knowing.

203
00:12:16,933 --> 00:12:19,991
All views and understanding
here are my own,

204
00:12:20,071 --> 00:12:22,423
from my practice and contemplation.

205
00:12:22,503 --> 00:12:26,504
I do not represent any
tradition, school or teacher.

206
00:12:27,318 --> 00:12:32,741
So what is it for? It explains, it
dismantles, and it describes the taste.

207
00:12:32,821 --> 00:12:36,178
It is the antidote to
ignorance, not its shape.

208
00:12:36,258 --> 00:12:39,919
And what veils is ignorance,
never dependent arising.

209
00:12:40,738 --> 00:12:45,065
Next: how it is met, as
a taste. That is Part 4.

